## Output Requirements

When calling `task_complete`, you MUST include a structured `discoveries` object with these fields so the orchestrator can process your findings:

```json
{
  "summary": "Brief description of findings",
  "discoveries": {
    "hosts": [
      {
        "ip": "10.1.2.100",
        "hostname": "dc01.contoso.local",
        "is_dc": true,
        "os": "Windows Server 2019",
        "services": [{"port": 445, "protocol": "tcp", "service": "microsoft-ds"}],
        "roles": ["AD DC"]
      }
    ],
    "discovered_users": [
      {"username": "jdoe", "domain": "contoso.local", "is_admin": false}
    ],
    "shares": [
      {"host": "10.1.2.100", "name": "SYSVOL", "permissions": "READ"}
    ],
    "vulnerabilities": [
      {
        "vuln_type": "mssql_impersonation",
        "target_ip": "10.1.2.100",
        "account_name": "svc_sql",
        "domain": "contoso.local",
        "details": "description"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

**Critical**: For hosts with Kerberos (88), LDAP (389), or DNS (53) services, set `is_dc: true` and include the full FQDN hostname (e.g. `dc01.contoso.local`). This triggers automated credential attacks.
